DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The library is used to simplify Capsicumizing a tools that are using file
     system.  Idea behind the library is that we are passing a remaining _a_r_g_c
     and _a_r_g_v which contains a list of files that should be open for this pro‐
     gram.  The library will create a service that will serve those files.

     The function ffiilleeaarrggss__iinniitt() create a service to the ssyysstteemm..ffiilleeaarrggss.
     The _a_r_g_v contains a list of files that should be opened.  The argument
     can be set to NULL which will not create a service and all files will be
     prohibited to be opened.  The _a_r_g_c argument contains a number of passed
     files.  The _f_l_a_g_s argument limits opened files for either execution or
     reading and/or writing.  The _m_o_d_e argument tells which what mode file
     should be created if the O_CREATE flag is present .  For more details of
     the _f_l_a_g_s and _m_o_d_e arguments see open(2).  The _r_i_g_h_t_s_p argument contains
     a list of the capability rights which file should be limited to.  For
     more details of the capability rights see cap_rights_init(3).  The
     _o_p_e_r_a_t_i_o_n_s argument limits the operations that are available using
     ssyysstteemm..ffiilleeaarrggss.  _o_p_e_r_a_t_i_o_n_s is a combination of:

           FA_OPEN
           Allow ffiilleeaarrggss__ooppeenn() and ffiilleeaarrggss__ffooppeenn().

           FA_LSTAT
           Allow ffiilleeaarrggss__llssttaatt().

           FA_REALPATH
           Allow ffiilleeaarrggss__rreeaallppaatthh().

     The function ffiilleeaarrggss__cciinniitt() is equivalent to ffiilleeaarrggss__iinniitt() except
     that the connection to the Casper needs to be provided.

     The functions ffiilleeaarrggss__iinniittnnvv() and ffiilleeaarrggss__cciinniittnnvv() are respectively
